$ Theta_b in "CH"^2 \( S_b^0 times X_b \)_(bb(Q)) $

 whose action on $U_b$ is the given identification with $H^2 \( X_b \)^(j = + \, thin delta = -)$.]
] <comp:surface>

#proof[
  The variation, the projector, and the identification are supplied by Proposition 3.1, Proposition 5.1. 17 gives the uniruled threefold models on the K3 side. For $X$, after $t = s + u^2$ the generic fiber over $B'$ is the conic
  $ z^2 - pi^(*) d_1 thin u^2 = pi^(*) \( d_0 + s d_1 \) $
  over $bb(C) \( B' \)$. A finite extension splits this conic, so a generically finite surface cover of $B'$ yields a dominant rational map from a product of a surface and $upright(bold(P))^1$. Every smooth projective model of the threefold is therefore uniruled. Theorem 23 applies. It applies separately to every fixed pencil with these properties; its countable set of excluded $b$ is chosen only after the pencil, the degree-three correspondence, and the good $s$-open have been fixed. ◻
